Yes. And after rerunning the idea against external work on requirements engineering, verification/validation, traceability, and instruction-following evaluation, I would upgrade the curriculum substantially. NASA's requirements guidance emphasizes clarity, completeness, consistency, verifiability, and bidirectional traceability; current LLM evaluation research similarly emphasizes objectively verifiable instructions and careful evaluation protocols. 

So let's build Instruction & Protocol Engineering School — v2.

The goal is not "learn how OC writes."

The goal is:

> Become capable of independently designing, criticizing, testing, and revising instructions and protocols for unfamiliar problems.




