STAGE IV — Evidence Engineering

This becomes the core of your particular methodology.

Level 15 — Evidence classification

We'll formally distinguish:

E0 — MODEL KNOWLEDGE

E1 — EXTERNAL / WEB EVIDENCE

E2 — IMPLEMENTATION EVIDENCE

E3 — EXPERIMENTAL EVIDENCE

E4 — ANALYTICAL INFERENCE

E5 — HYPOTHESIS

E6 — SUPPORTED CONCLUSION

And we'll practice refusing to promote one category into another.

For example:

> "The code contains a regex."



Implementation evidence.

> "The regex matched 8/12 test cases."



Experimental evidence.

> "The regex is probably causing false positives."



Hypothesis.

Not the same thing.


---

Level 16 — Evidence provenance

Every important claim should answer:

WHERE DID THIS COME FROM?

Possible answers:

